Imports:
  - Types:
      - Exchange
    From: freqtrade/exchange

Annotations: |
  `DataProvider` is the read-only market-data facade strategies and other cells use instead of
  talking to `Exchange` directly — it adds caching, backtesting/live-mode switching, and
  producer/consumer data sharing on top of the raw `Exchange` calls.

---

"DataProvider(config: dict[str, Any], exchange: Exchange | None, pairlists: Any, rpc: Any)":
  location: dataprovider.py
  annotations: |
    exchange: live `Exchange` to read market data from; `None` in exchange-less analysis
    contexts, in which case exchange-backed methods raise OperationalException
    `pairlists`: the pairlist manager currently in effect (left untyped here to avoid a cell
    import cycle with freqtrade/plugins; treated as an opaque handle by this cell)
    rpc: optional RPC manager used by send_msg
  properties:
    "runmode -> RunMode": |
      The run mode (live/dry-run/backtest/hyperopt/...) this `DataProvider` is operating under.
    "available_pairs -> list[tuple[str, str, str]]": |
      (pair, timeframe, candle_type) tuples currently cached and available for lookup.
  methods:
    "historic_ohlcv(pair: str, timeframe: str, candle_type: str) -> candles:DataFrame": |
      Load historical OHLCV candles for `pair` from local storage (not the live exchange).
    "get_pair_dataframe(pair: str, timeframe: str | None, candle_type: str) -> candles:DataFrame": |
      Return the best available OHLCV DataFrame for `pair`/`timeframe` — live cache if running
      live/dry-run, historical file data otherwise.
    "get_analyzed_dataframe(pair: str, timeframe: str) -> result:tuple[DataFrame, datetime]": |
      Return the strategy-analyzed (post populate_indicators) DataFrame for `pair`, plus the
      timestamp it was last analyzed.

      `result`: (dataframe, last_analyzed_datetime)
    "refresh(pairlist: list[tuple[str, str, str]], helping_pairs: list[tuple[str, str, str]] | None)": |
      Refresh the OHLCV cache for every pair/timeframe in `pairlist` (and `helping_pairs`, e.g.
      informative pairs) from exchange.
    "ohlcv(pair: str, timeframe: str | None, copy: bool, candle_type: str) -> candles:DataFrame": |
      Return the raw (not strategy-analyzed) cached OHLCV DataFrame for `pair`.
    "trades(pair: str, timeframe: str | None, copy: bool, candle_type: str, timerange: Any | None) -> trades:DataFrame": |
      Return cached/historical trade-level (tick) data for `pair`, where available.
    "market(pair: str) -> market:dict[str, Any] | None": |
      Return the raw ccxt market dict for `pair` via exchange, or `None` if unknown.
    "orderbook(pair: str, maximum: int) -> book:dict[str, Any]": |
      Fetch the current order book for `pair`, limited to `maximum` levels per side.
    "send_msg(message: str, always_send: bool)": |
      Forward a notification to rpc, deduplicating repeated messages unless `always_send`.

